WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:27.160
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:27.430 --> 01:34.920
[The Great Long March]

3
01:35.259 --> 01:37.820
[Episode 30]

4
01:38.530 --> 01:40.620
[Ya'an, Sichuan]

5
01:38.590 --> 01:39.310
Uncle.

6
01:40.400 --> 01:41.310
You came just at the right time. Uncle.

7
01:41.310 --> 01:43.370
The hotpot is almost ready. Sit down.

8
01:43.630 --> 01:45.920
Uncle, at a time like this,

9
01:46.210 --> 01:48.210
you're still in the mood for hotpot?

10
01:52.930 --> 01:53.479
Here.

11
01:55.229 --> 01:56.000
Damn it.

12
01:57.850 --> 01:59.200
When a person is out of luck,

13
01:58.420 --> 02:00.470
[Liu Yuantang; Liu Wenhui's nephew, Commander of the 1st Brigade of the KMT's Chuan-Kang Frontier Force]

14
01:59.460 --> 02:01.160
even drinking water can make them choke.

15
02:01.160 --> 02:01.830
Uncle.

16
02:02.440 --> 02:04.440
We fought Liu Xiang for so many years

17
02:04.550 --> 02:06.700
and finally got to Xikang to take a breather.

18
02:06.700 --> 02:09.090
Why is the Communist Army coming right at us?

19
02:09.090 --> 02:09.880
Exactly.

20
02:11.290 --> 02:13.170
Uncle, say something.

21
02:16.750 --> 02:19.350
You can't eat hot tofu in a hurry.

22
02:20.640 --> 02:21.170
Here,

23
02:21.200 --> 02:22.530
have some garlic paste.

24
02:25.090 --> 02:25.950
That's enough.

25
02:27.770 --> 02:31.680
[Liu Wenhui; Commander-in-Chief of the KMT's Chuan-Kang Frontier Force and Commander of the KMT's 24th Army]

26
02:28.780 --> 02:30.110
This telegram of Chiang

27
02:30.750 --> 02:32.030
is like hot tofu.

28
02:32.400 --> 02:34.750
You can't swallow it, nor can you spit it out.

29
02:34.750 --> 02:35.910
It burns your mouth.

30
02:37.200 --> 02:38.829
Uncle, if you ask me,

31
02:39.020 --> 02:41.940
the best move would be to have Xue Yue and Long Yun

32
02:42.140 --> 02:45.970
[Liu Yuanzhang; Liu Wenhui's nephew, Commander of KMT's Chuan-Kang Frontier Force]

33
02:42.250 --> 02:44.130
block the Communist Army on the south bank.

34
02:44.130 --> 02:44.940
That way,

35
02:44.970 --> 02:46.370
they won't even bother crossing the river.

36
02:46.370 --> 02:48.910
If the Communist Army were really that weak,

37
02:49.120 --> 02:50.610
they wouldn't have made it all the way from Jiangxi

38
02:50.610 --> 02:51.930
to the Jinsha River.

39
02:52.150 --> 02:54.560
So do we defend or not?

40
02:55.320 --> 02:57.190
If you have a piece of tofu in your mouth

41
02:57.190 --> 02:59.030
and it burns your mouth, what do you do?

42
02:59.030 --> 02:59.840
Spit it out.

43
03:00.210 --> 03:01.680
That's a waste of food.

44
03:01.710 --> 03:03.830
Soak it in sesame oil for a bit.

45
03:05.310 --> 03:06.870
We still have to defend.

46
03:07.020 --> 03:09.700
We can't give Chiang anything to use against us.

47
03:11.180 --> 03:12.710
We only have so many troops.

48
03:12.820 --> 03:14.080
We can't lose them all.

49
03:14.430 --> 03:15.290
How about this?

50
03:17.910 --> 03:19.190
We, the 24th Army,

51
03:21.670 --> 03:23.390
will set up two lines of defense,

52
03:23.390 --> 03:25.050
the first at the Jinsha River,

53
03:25.280 --> 03:27.079
and the second at the Dadu River.

54
03:27.120 --> 03:29.280
The first line of defense is mainly to defend the city,

55
03:29.280 --> 03:30.640
and secondarily to defend the river.

56
03:30.640 --> 03:32.630
Regarding the defense of the river…

57
03:32.630 --> 03:33.520
Yuantang.

58
03:33.880 --> 03:36.410
Take three regiments and the local militias,

59
03:37.190 --> 03:38.430
drag over all the boats from both sides of the river

60
03:38.430 --> 03:39.680
and burn them.

61
03:40.360 --> 03:42.120
Carry out a scorched-earth policy

62
03:42.120 --> 03:43.480
and hold out for a few days.

63
03:43.480 --> 03:45.790
When the Central Army arrives, we'll have done our part.

64
03:45.790 --> 03:46.829
I understand.

65
03:47.420 --> 03:50.550
The most important thing is to wait for the Central Army.

66
03:55.360 --> 03:56.560
You eat first, Uncle.

67
03:56.930 --> 03:58.200
I'll go make arrangements right away.

68
03:58.200 --> 03:59.280
What's the rush?

69
04:00.240 --> 04:02.000
The line of defense of the river is so long.

70
04:02.000 --> 04:03.010
Where's the focus?

71
04:03.010 --> 04:04.670
Where will the main forces be?

72
04:04.760 --> 04:06.350
Explain it to Uncle.

73
04:10.470 --> 04:12.070
If I were the Communist Army,

74
04:13.630 --> 04:15.800
my first choice would be to cross the river at Qiaojia

75
04:15.800 --> 04:17.829
and attack Xichang via Ningnan.

76
04:18.070 --> 04:20.040
This is the area where it's easiest to cross the river

77
04:20.040 --> 04:22.480
and the most advantageous for the Communist Army to move north.

78
04:22.480 --> 04:24.390
So I would put the main forces of river defense

79
04:24.390 --> 04:25.800
in this direction.

80
04:26.830 --> 04:28.430
Of course, besides Qiaojia,

81
04:28.560 --> 04:30.950
the Communist Army might also cross the river from Jiangyi.

82
04:30.950 --> 04:33.120
The mountain roads of that area are hard to navigate.

83
04:33.120 --> 04:34.970
I'll put another regiment there to guard it,

84
04:34.970 --> 04:35.930
just to be safe.

85
04:36.250 --> 04:37.930
How's that, Uncle, Brother?

86
04:38.110 --> 04:40.260
Is it a good plan?

87
04:41.490 --> 04:43.240
Yuantang, you've improved.

88
04:43.600 --> 04:44.310
It's good.

89
04:44.350 --> 04:45.680
I'll do it this way then.

90
04:50.270 --> 04:57.159
[Longjie Ferry, Jinsha River, Yunnan]

91
04:50.500 --> 04:51.500
Give me a hand.

92
04:55.730 --> 04:57.000
Be careful.

93
04:57.270 --> 04:57.800
Okay.

94
04:58.120 --> 04:59.030
While ensuring safety,

95
04:59.030 --> 05:00.200
move faster.

96
05:01.360 --> 05:02.560
Come on. Move faster.

97
05:04.190 --> 05:04.920
Put it down.

98
05:05.870 --> 05:07.160
Keep up. Keep up!

99
05:07.180 --> 05:07.980
Hold on tight.

100
05:09.680 --> 05:11.150
Be careful. Be careful.

101
05:11.170 --> 05:12.220
Watch out!

102
05:16.860 --> 05:17.770
Excuse me.

103
05:20.040 --> 05:20.900
Here, put it here.

104
05:20.900 --> 05:21.870
Tie it tighter.

105
05:22.190 --> 05:23.250
Move them all here.

106
05:24.000 --> 05:26.400
There are more here. Send a few more people.

107
05:27.250 --> 05:27.960
Come on.

108
05:32.570 --> 05:33.300
Tie it tight.

109
05:34.120 --> 05:35.430
Come on. Give me a hand.

110
05:35.430 --> 05:37.030
Second Squad, go over there.

111
05:37.040 --> 05:37.480
Okay.

112
05:39.450 --> 05:40.250
Hold on tight.

113
05:46.010 --> 05:47.400
Put down everything in your hands!

114
05:47.400 --> 05:49.260
There are enemy planes! Retreat!

115
05:49.310 --> 05:50.480
Retreat! Get down and take cover!

116
05:50.480 --> 05:51.040
Hurry!

117
05:51.340 --> 05:52.180
Retreat!

118
05:52.490 --> 05:53.960
Hurry! Retreat!

119
05:57.140 --> 05:57.700
Hurry!

120
05:58.240 --> 05:58.900
Take cover!

121
05:59.640 --> 06:00.990
Move fast! Take cover!

122
06:01.800 --> 06:02.390
Go!

123
06:03.950 --> 06:05.360
Get down!

124
07:01.130 --> 07:02.850
[Yang Chengwu, Political Commissar of the 4th Regiment, 2nd Division, 1st Red Army Corps]

125
07:02.970 --> 07:05.900
[Mao Zhenhua, Company Commander of the 3rd Company, 1st Battalion, 4th Regiment]

126
07:15.000 --> 07:18.320
[Longjie Village, Yuanmou, Yunnan; Temporary Headquarters of the 1st Red Army Corps]

127
07:17.860 --> 07:20.390
Here. Put this next to the bamboo pole.

128
07:22.000 --> 07:23.290
Watch your step.

129
07:24.160 --> 07:26.070
We've searched dozens of miles along the shore,

130
07:26.070 --> 07:27.350
and there's not a single boat.

131
07:27.350 --> 07:28.310
The enemy planes keep harassing us.

132
07:28.310 --> 07:29.040
At this rate,

133
07:29.080 --> 07:31.410
we'll never get the pontoon bridge built.

134
07:34.220 --> 07:37.390
[Lin Biao, Commander of the 1st Red Army Corps]

135
07:51.930 --> 07:54.730
Isn't it much easier to cross at Qiaojia than here?

136
07:57.980 --> 07:59.130
The Military Commission's deployment

137
07:59.010 --> 08:03.500
[Nie Rongzhen, Political Commissar of the 1st Red Army Corps]

138
07:59.320 --> 08:01.320
was made after full consideration.

139
08:01.850 --> 08:04.070
If we run into difficulties in execution,

140
08:04.070 --> 08:06.370
we just need to report the actual situation.

141
08:06.370 --> 08:08.970
We still have to find a way to complete the task.

142
08:26.040 --> 08:32.450
[Jiepai Village, Luquan, Yunnan]

143
08:27.110 --> 08:28.320
The 1st Red Army Corps reported

144
08:28.320 --> 08:29.460
that the enemy air force

145
08:29.460 --> 08:31.950
has already gathered intelligence on their bridge construction.

146
08:31.950 --> 08:33.080
They were harassed multiple times a day

147
08:33.080 --> 08:35.240
and simply can't build the pontoon bridge at all.

148
08:35.240 --> 08:37.419
The pontoon bridge of the 3rd Red Army Corps at Hongmen Ferry

149
08:37.419 --> 08:39.350
was swept away right after it was built.

150
08:39.350 --> 08:41.539
Currently, they've only found one small wooden boat.

151
08:41.539 --> 08:42.440
If the whole Corps

152
08:42.440 --> 08:44.179
relies on this one small wooden boat to cross the river,

153
08:44.179 --> 08:46.240
it will take at least ten days or more.

154
08:46.560 --> 08:48.640
The Second Bureau just decoded an enemy telegram.

155
08:48.640 --> 08:49.860
Chiang Kai-shek's troops

156
08:49.860 --> 08:51.510
are rushing towards the Jinsha River.

157
08:51.510 --> 08:53.710
If we can't cross the river on schedule,

158
08:54.040 --> 08:55.660
then the time we bought earlier

159
08:55.660 --> 08:56.720
will all be wasted.

160
08:57.320 --> 08:58.480
It's a do-or-die battle.

161
08:58.480 --> 09:00.410
We don't even have a way to retreat.

162
09:01.240 --> 09:03.750
The time to cross the river must not be delayed.

163
09:03.750 --> 09:05.050
No matter how big the difficulties are,

164
09:05.050 --> 09:06.310
we must overcome them.

165
09:06.910 --> 09:08.150
If we cannot cross

166
09:08.390 --> 09:09.870
at Longjie Ferry or Hongmen Ferry,

167
09:09.870 --> 09:10.970
we still have Jiaoping Ferry.

168
09:10.970 --> 09:11.640
Right.

169
09:12.030 --> 09:12.750
I propose

170
09:12.800 --> 09:14.840
that we immediately form a river-crossing advance unit.

171
09:14.840 --> 09:17.260
The commander of the advance unit will still be our "Dragon King,"

172
09:17.260 --> 09:18.260
Comrade Bocheng.

173
09:18.320 --> 09:18.960
Yes, sir.

174
09:19.210 --> 09:21.440
The task of the river-crossing advance unit

175
09:21.440 --> 09:22.790
will be handed over to the Cadre Regiment.

176
09:22.790 --> 09:24.440
In addition, we can send Comrade Li Kenong

177
09:24.440 --> 09:25.300
with a working group

178
09:25.300 --> 09:26.900
to assist them in execution.

179
09:27.910 --> 09:28.550
Good.

180
09:28.570 --> 09:29.930
Then, should the operations of the 1st and 3rd Red Army Corps

181
09:29.930 --> 09:31.410
be paused for now?

182
09:31.550 --> 09:32.360
Don't pause.

183
09:32.600 --> 09:33.630
Since they've already figured out

184
09:33.630 --> 09:34.490
our direction,

185
09:34.670 --> 09:36.610
we should continue to reinforce their judgment.

186
09:36.610 --> 09:38.660
When the fake is taken for real, the real becomes fake.

187
09:38.660 --> 09:42.320
Where nothing is taken as something, something becomes nothing.

188
09:46.780 --> 09:51.750
[Jiepai Village, Luquan, Yunnan; Encampment of the Cadre Regiment]

189
09:49.270 --> 09:50.000
Xiao.

190
09:50.270 --> 09:51.270
I've noticed

191
09:51.600 --> 09:53.800
that your 5th Company has the most lice.

192
09:54.400 --> 09:55.520
Regiment Commander.

193
09:55.520 --> 09:56.760
As the saying goes,

194
09:56.820 --> 09:59.520
[Xiao Yingtang, Company Commander of the 5th Company of the 2nd Battalion of the Cadre Regiment of Military Commission Column]

195
09:58.550 --> 10:00.270
Idle people get lice; lazy people get sick.

196
10:00.270 --> 10:01.870
Our company has a lot of lice.

197
10:01.870 --> 10:03.550
That's because we've been idle.

198
10:03.550 --> 10:04.510
Xiao Yingtang.

199
10:05.130 --> 10:05.970
Here.

200
10:06.680 --> 10:08.290
What you said

201
10:10.510 --> 10:11.750
is very well put.

202
10:13.220 --> 10:14.290
You scared me.

203
10:14.720 --> 10:15.740
I've learned something.

204
10:15.740 --> 10:16.340
Next time,

205
10:16.340 --> 10:18.280
when I see the leader of the Military Commission,

206
10:18.280 --> 10:19.010
I'll say the same thing.

207
10:19.010 --> 10:20.010
And I'll tell you,

208
10:20.070 --> 10:20.920
I learned this

209
10:21.220 --> 10:22.650
from Xiao Yingtang.

210
10:23.240 --> 10:24.300
Don't say I said it.

211
10:24.320 --> 10:25.440
I'll definitely say that.

212
10:25.440 --> 10:26.630
If you put it that way,

213
10:26.630 --> 10:27.960
then the idlest person in our regiment

214
10:27.960 --> 10:29.490
is the Regiment Commander.

215
10:29.960 --> 10:30.980
You guys don't know.

216
10:30.980 --> 10:33.090
[Song Renqiong, Political Commissar of the Cadre Regiment of the Military Commission Column]

217
10:31.120 --> 10:32.270
Just now, I threw his shirt

218
10:32.270 --> 10:33.360
into that pot.

219
10:33.630 --> 10:34.490
What happened?

220
10:34.940 --> 10:36.240
The smell of boiled lice

221
10:36.240 --> 10:38.190
rose right up.

222
10:39.000 --> 10:40.150
That smell

223
10:40.290 --> 10:42.420
was exactly like that of braised pork.

224
10:42.870 --> 10:43.500
Did you count them?

225
10:43.500 --> 10:45.040
Was it 57 or 58 lice?

226
10:45.390 --> 10:46.550
I did, 58.

227
10:46.770 --> 10:47.970
I'll serve you a bowl.

228
10:49.000 --> 10:49.710
Chen Geng.

229
10:51.170 --> 10:51.930
Vice Chairman Zhou.

230
10:51.790 --> 10:54.360
[Chen Geng, Regiment Commander of the Cadre Regiment of the Military Commission Column]

231
10:52.350 --> 10:53.680
Comrade Chief of Staff.

232
10:54.900 --> 10:56.090
What are you doing?

233
10:57.120 --> 10:59.910
Some companies of the Cadre Regiment are conducting

234
10:59.910 --> 11:01.130
a lice-boiling operation.

235
11:01.130 --> 11:02.390
Awaiting your orders.

236
11:04.270 --> 11:05.660
There is an important task

237
11:05.660 --> 11:07.440
to be assigned to your Cadre Regiment.

238
11:07.440 --> 11:07.970
Yes, sir.

239
11:08.310 --> 11:09.640
Leader, please come in.

240
11:10.440 --> 11:10.810
Hello, Leader.

241
11:10.810 --> 11:11.270
Hurry up.

242
11:11.270 --> 11:11.650
Hello, Leader.

243
11:11.650 --> 11:12.090
Yes, sir.

244
11:12.090 --> 11:13.820
You guys continue your operation.

245
11:13.820 --> 11:15.060
Yes, sir.

246
11:19.830 --> 11:21.830
The current situation is like this.

247
11:22.470 --> 11:24.900
The 1st and 3rd Red Army Corps failed to build the pontoon bridge,

248
11:24.900 --> 11:26.830
so they have to rush back to Jiaoping Ferry to cross the river.

249
11:26.830 --> 11:28.610
To ensure that the main forces of the Red Army

250
11:28.610 --> 11:30.790
cross the natural barrier completely and smoothly,

251
11:30.790 --> 11:31.830
the Military Commission has decided

252
11:31.830 --> 11:34.370
to send the Cadre Regiment as the river-crossing advance unit

253
11:34.370 --> 11:36.680
to quickly seize the Jiaoping Ferry.

254
11:38.010 --> 11:38.630
Is that clear?

255
11:38.630 --> 11:39.840
Please rest assured, leaders of the Military Commission.

256
11:39.840 --> 11:40.850
We guarantee we'll complete the mission!

257
11:40.850 --> 11:42.230
We'll complete the mission!

258
11:42.230 --> 11:44.990
Comrade Bocheng, please introduce the specific situation.

259
11:44.990 --> 11:46.630
The key to this mission

260
11:46.960 --> 11:49.290
is to find as many ferry boats as possible.

261
11:49.600 --> 11:50.430
Besides the ferry boats,

262
11:50.430 --> 11:53.040
we also need to get as many local boatmen as possible

263
11:53.040 --> 11:55.350
[Li Kenong, Chief of Work Department of the Red Army of the National Security Bureau]

264
11:53.190 --> 11:54.620
to ferry us across the river.

265
11:54.620 --> 11:55.350
In addition,

266
11:55.430 --> 11:57.000
We're still over 200 li of mountain road

267
11:57.000 --> 11:58.510
away from Jiaoping Ferry.

268
11:58.910 --> 12:00.440
Considering the complex enemy situation

269
12:00.440 --> 12:01.230
and tight schedule,

270
12:01.230 --> 12:03.160
a large troop movement might attract

271
12:03.160 --> 12:04.130
the enemy's attention

272
12:04.130 --> 12:05.700
and cause unnecessary trouble.

273
12:05.700 --> 12:07.390
So I hope your Cadre Regiment

274
12:07.410 --> 12:08.620
can send one company

275
12:08.870 --> 12:11.000
as an advance detachment to make a rapid march

276
12:11.000 --> 12:12.480
and reach the ferry first.

277
12:12.960 --> 12:14.310
We guarantee we'll complete the mission.

278
12:14.310 --> 12:16.260
Then which company do you plan to send

279
12:16.260 --> 12:17.660
to execute this mission?

280
12:22.680 --> 12:24.910
Let's send the 5th Company of the 2nd Battalion.

281
12:24.910 --> 12:26.340
The Company Commander is Xiao Yingtang,

282
12:26.340 --> 12:27.610
a veteran of the Red Army.

283
12:27.610 --> 12:29.120
He had fought in Tucheng and the Xiang River,

284
12:29.120 --> 12:30.250
and he did a good job.

285
12:30.810 --> 12:31.360
Okay.

286
12:32.360 --> 12:33.690
To ensure the mission goes smoothly,

287
12:33.690 --> 12:35.400
the Military Commission has dispatched Comrade Li Kenong

288
12:35.400 --> 12:36.810
with a working group

289
12:36.880 --> 12:38.580
to operate alongside you.

290
12:39.810 --> 12:41.070
Then he is not welcome.

291
12:42.000 --> 12:42.800
Just kidding.

292
12:43.000 --> 12:44.140
Welcome, welcome, welcome.

293
12:44.140 --> 12:45.430
He and I are old partners.

294
12:45.430 --> 12:45.910
Yes.

295
12:45.930 --> 12:47.370
We will definitely complete the mission.

296
12:47.370 --> 12:48.640
I can prove that.

297
12:49.020 --> 12:49.730
In 1930,

298
12:50.010 --> 12:51.430
it was you two who worked together

299
12:51.430 --> 12:52.470
to escort me safely

300
12:52.470 --> 12:53.950
from Shanghai to Wuhan.

301
12:54.480 --> 12:55.210
That's true.

302
12:55.480 --> 12:56.030
Have you forgotten?

303
12:56.030 --> 12:57.100
The one who assigned us the mission back then

304
12:57.100 --> 12:58.310
was Comrade Wu Hao (Zhou Enlai).

305
12:58.310 --> 12:59.140
Right, right.

306
12:59.910 --> 13:00.840
I hope this time

307
13:01.030 --> 13:02.640
we can cooperate wholeheartedly again

308
13:02.640 --> 13:04.910
and smoothly complete this arduous mission.

309
13:04.910 --> 13:05.870
Yes, sir!

310
13:06.170 --> 13:08.730
Reporting, leaders! Fifth Company has assembled!

311
13:08.730 --> 13:09.850
That was fast.

312
13:09.960 --> 13:12.110
Chen Geng, you're still so vigorous and resolute.

313
13:12.110 --> 13:12.890
Leaders, this way.

314
13:12.890 --> 13:13.300
Okay.

315
13:13.960 --> 13:14.390
Come.

316
13:14.410 --> 13:14.860
Come.

317
13:16.790 --> 13:17.840
What are the odds!

318
13:17.860 --> 13:18.790
We meet again.

319
13:23.850 --> 13:24.690
Leader.

320
13:31.870 --> 13:32.730
Whole Company,

321
13:32.910 --> 13:34.270
attention!

322
13:45.730 --> 13:47.420
Comrades, hear my orders.

323
13:47.830 --> 13:49.110
Take off

324
13:49.230 --> 13:50.430
all your wet clothes.

325
13:52.600 --> 13:53.800
Take off our clothes?

326
13:54.040 --> 13:54.890
Why?

327
13:55.850 --> 13:57.510
What are you surprised about?

328
13:59.620 --> 14:01.150
Dry them before you set off.

329
14:01.760 --> 14:02.890
Yes, sir!

330
14:05.940 --> 14:10.830
[Huize County (formerly known as Dongchuan), Yunnan]

331
14:15.550 --> 14:16.550
Corps Commander.

332
14:16.590 --> 14:17.850
Political Commissar.

333
14:18.750 --> 14:19.550
How is the situation?

334
14:19.550 --> 14:20.520
The city wall is too high.

335
14:20.520 --> 14:22.130
The morning attack didn't work.

336
14:22.130 --> 14:23.750
We've already surrounded the county town on three sides

337
14:23.750 --> 14:26.080
and can launch another attack at any time.

338
14:27.310 --> 14:30.180
[Xu Wenlie, Publicity Secretary of the Political Department of the 9th Red Army Corps]

339
14:27.550 --> 14:28.360
Secretary Xu.

340
14:28.630 --> 14:29.410
Corps Commander.

341
14:29.410 --> 14:30.570
You are a local.

342
14:30.330 --> 14:33.630
[Luo Binghui, Commander of the 9th Red Army Corps]

343
14:31.030 --> 14:34.150
Between the people of Xuanwei and the people of Dongchuan,

344
14:34.150 --> 14:35.370
whose lives are harder?

345
14:35.370 --> 14:36.610
Dongchuan produces copper

346
14:36.610 --> 14:37.740
and has a ferry port.

347
14:38.080 --> 14:40.100
There're more rich people than in Xuanwei.

348
14:40.100 --> 14:43.100
But the common people in Dongchuan live a harder life.

349
14:43.930 --> 14:44.570
Why?

350
14:44.750 --> 14:46.630
Yang Maozhang, the county magistrate of Dongchuan,

351
14:46.630 --> 14:48.300
and the local tyrant Liu Shanchu

352
14:48.300 --> 14:49.510
collude with each other.

353
14:49.510 --> 14:51.170
They treat the people like beasts of burden

354
14:51.170 --> 14:52.920
and force them to dig soil in the mountains every day.

355
14:52.920 --> 14:54.520
They don't care if the people live or die.

356
14:54.520 --> 14:56.450
I see the defenders on the city wall

357
14:57.120 --> 14:58.520
are all common people.

358
14:59.040 --> 15:01.160
They might not fight us to the death.

359
15:01.480 --> 15:02.450
Comrade Binghui,

360
15:02.450 --> 15:04.850
I see you want to fight a psychological war.

361
15:07.250 --> 15:08.840
Corps Commander, it's dangerous!

362
15:08.840 --> 15:09.440
It's fine.

363
15:11.030 --> 15:11.820
I'll go with you.

364
15:11.820 --> 15:12.550
No need.

365
15:13.140 --> 15:14.750
[He Changgong, Political Commissar of the 9th Red Army Corps]

366
15:13.280 --> 15:14.010
Binghui,

367
15:14.320 --> 15:15.210
be careful.

368
15:17.670 --> 15:19.130
Ready to fight at any time!

369
15:20.920 --> 15:22.640
Fellow villagers!

370
15:23.130 --> 15:24.440
Our Corps Commander

371
15:24.740 --> 15:26.980
wants to say a few words to you.

372
15:29.730 --> 15:30.850
Fellow villagers!

373
15:31.480 --> 15:32.840
I am Luo Binghui

374
15:33.280 --> 15:34.480
from Yiliang County.

375
15:35.480 --> 15:36.600
I am now

376
15:37.160 --> 15:39.190
standing within the range

377
15:39.210 --> 15:40.610
of your Hanyang rifles.

378
15:41.550 --> 15:42.590
But I believe

379
15:43.010 --> 15:45.040
you won't shoot.

380
15:46.120 --> 15:48.440
Because you are also poor people.

381
15:49.270 --> 15:50.300
I know

382
15:50.320 --> 15:52.750
you were threatened by Yang Maozhang and Liu Shanchu

383
15:52.750 --> 15:53.510
to come

384
15:54.200 --> 15:56.800
and risk your lives to defend the city for them.

385
15:57.400 --> 15:59.680
Are you doing this willingly?

386
16:01.010 --> 16:04.280
Do you think it's worth it?

387
16:04.720 --> 16:06.360
If you die,

388
16:06.750 --> 16:08.810
will they take pity on your families?

389
16:09.100 --> 16:10.220
No.

390
16:10.800 --> 16:12.240
What will happen to your parents,

391
16:12.240 --> 16:13.080
wife,

392
16:13.100 --> 16:14.500
and children?

393
16:14.750 --> 16:17.080
They will only live a harder life.

394
16:17.820 --> 16:21.530
I hope you'll search your conscience and think about it.

395
16:22.470 --> 16:24.800
Does what I said make sense?

396
16:24.890 --> 16:25.970
Is it right?

397
16:26.040 --> 16:27.840
Fellow villagers of Dongchuan,

398
16:28.390 --> 16:29.920
I am Xu Wenlie from Xuanwei.

399
16:30.310 --> 16:31.350
You must have heard about

400
16:31.350 --> 16:32.810
what happened in Xuanwei.

401
16:32.870 --> 16:34.320
After the Red Army entered the city,

402
16:34.320 --> 16:34.960
they did not

403
16:34.960 --> 16:36.690
give a single ordinary person a hard time.

404
16:36.690 --> 16:39.230
They even distributed the rich family's money,

405
16:39.230 --> 16:43.270
grain, and ham to the poor.

406
16:43.770 --> 16:46.800
The Red Army is an army that fights for the poor.

407
16:47.000 --> 16:48.000
Don't be accomplices

408
16:48.000 --> 16:50.630
of Yang Maozhang and Liu Shanchu anymore.

409
16:50.820 --> 16:51.780
Look at

410
16:51.800 --> 16:53.430
how many Red Army soldiers are outside the city.

411
16:53.430 --> 16:54.540
If we really attack the city,

412
16:54.540 --> 16:55.870
can you hold it?

413
16:55.890 --> 16:59.150
We haven't attacked you because we don't want to scare you.

414
16:59.680 --> 17:02.480
Fellow villagers, I, Luo Binghui,

415
17:03.070 --> 17:05.300
come from a poor family too.

416
17:06.030 --> 17:08.520
My family has been tenant farmers for generations.

417
17:08.520 --> 17:10.800
I started working in the fields at the age of five.

418
17:10.800 --> 17:12.430
The landlords called us

419
17:13.180 --> 17:14.510
"slave kids."

420
17:14.980 --> 17:16.069
Right?

421
17:16.089 --> 17:18.720
I worked like a beast of burden for them all year round,

422
17:18.720 --> 17:20.200
without enough food or warm clothes.

423
17:20.200 --> 17:21.400
I was beaten every day,

424
17:21.400 --> 17:24.060
living worse than a dog in the landlord's house.

425
17:24.640 --> 17:25.510
At the age of 16,

426
17:26.060 --> 17:28.590
I was persecuted by the landlord and ran away.

427
17:28.630 --> 17:30.320
I've mined coal,

428
17:30.580 --> 17:31.910
worked as a bricklayer,

429
17:32.580 --> 17:35.380
and even risked my life for the warlord Tang Jiyao.

430
17:35.770 --> 17:37.570
Later I realized one thing:

431
17:37.770 --> 17:40.900
The warlords and the rich landlords are in the same gang.

432
17:41.260 --> 17:44.020
They do things that bleed people dry.

433
17:45.270 --> 17:47.880
Later, I joined the Red Army.

434
17:48.440 --> 17:49.720
The Red Army

435
17:50.560 --> 17:53.640
is an army that fights for the poor.

436
17:54.880 --> 17:58.200
It is our own army, the army of the poor.

437
17:58.390 --> 18:00.750
People like that dog of a county magistrate Yang Maozhang

438
18:00.750 --> 18:03.010
and the tyrannical landlord Liu Shanchu

439
18:03.010 --> 18:04.740
are all enemies of the Red Army.

440
18:04.920 --> 18:06.250
Now the Red Army is here,

441
18:06.720 --> 18:08.310
they're done for.

442
18:08.400 --> 18:09.460
Fellow villagers,

443
18:10.110 --> 18:12.150
please believe me, Luo Binghui.

444
18:12.610 --> 18:15.670
When the Red Army attacks the county town of Dongchuan,

445
18:15.700 --> 18:18.090
we'll only kill that dog of a county magistrate Yang Maozhang

446
18:18.090 --> 18:19.750
and the landlord Liu Shanchu.

447
18:19.750 --> 18:21.960
If you open the city gates and surrender

448
18:22.160 --> 18:23.590
before we attack,

449
18:24.100 --> 18:25.620
we absolutely won't harm

450
18:25.650 --> 18:27.320
a single ordinary person.

451
18:28.000 --> 18:29.920
We will do the same as we did in Xuanwei.

452
18:29.920 --> 18:30.870
Don't listen to him.

453
18:30.870 --> 18:32.110
He's lying to you.

454
18:44.330 --> 18:46.490
Corps Commander, it's getting dark soon.

455
18:46.490 --> 18:47.290
Let's attack.

456
18:47.660 --> 18:48.860
Wait a little longer.

457
19:18.980 --> 19:19.590
Leave.

458
19:34.010 --> 19:36.310
On May 3, 1935,

459
19:36.870 --> 19:39.140
the 9th Red Army Corps took Huize (formerly known as Dongchuan)

460
19:39.140 --> 19:40.930
without a battle.

461
19:41.900 --> 19:43.850
This operation by the 9th Red Army Corps

462
19:43.850 --> 19:46.910
successfully disrupted Chiang Kai-shek's judgment,

463
19:46.940 --> 19:49.140
dispersed the forces of the KMT troops,

464
19:49.620 --> 19:52.890
and relieved the pressure on the main forces of the Central Red Army.

465
19:52.890 --> 19:54.120
It bought strategic space and time

466
19:54.120 --> 19:56.270
for the main forces

467
19:56.290 --> 19:59.180
to finally cross the Jinsha River smoothly.

468
20:04.090 --> 20:08.580
[Luquan, Yunnan; Encampment of the Second Bureau of Military Commission]

469
20:24.610 --> 20:25.570
This Long Yun.

470
20:26.270 --> 20:27.400
Of all times,

471
20:27.570 --> 20:30.430
he chose to change the codebook at this very moment.

472
20:30.480 --> 20:31.130
What?

473
20:30.680 --> 20:32.940
[Cao Xiangren, Section Chief of the Second Bureau of Central Revolutionary Military Commission]

474
20:31.230 --> 20:33.290
Does Long Yun have to ask for your permission

475
20:33.290 --> 20:36.090
before changing his codebook, Section Chief Cao?

476
20:36.330 --> 20:36.890
Zeng,

477
20:37.040 --> 20:38.700
I'm in no mood to joke with you.

478
20:39.310 --> 20:41.680
Do I look like I'm joking with you?

479
20:41.760 --> 20:43.700
If you don't want to give in to Long Yun,

480
20:43.700 --> 20:44.720
then sit down

481
20:44.790 --> 20:46.680
[Zeng Xisheng, Director of the Second Bureau of Central Revolutionary Military Commission]

482
20:44.990 --> 20:47.070
and decipher his codebook.

483
20:53.860 --> 20:55.140
Fine. Just watch me.

484
21:04.440 --> 21:07.110
Losing your temper can't solve any problem.

485
21:08.720 --> 21:10.380
I just got heated for a moment.

486
21:12.400 --> 21:15.200
When Vice Chairman Zhou came to ask about the decryption progress earlier,

487
21:15.200 --> 21:17.700
who was it that brushed him off?

488
21:18.940 --> 21:21.590
I've been upset about this all along.

489
21:22.200 --> 21:24.850
Only by deciphering Long Yun's code

490
21:25.100 --> 21:27.300
can we make his all-night wait worth it.

491
22:09.790 --> 22:11.990
Why is there still no news from Bocheng?

492
22:12.160 --> 22:13.440
He should be on his way.

493
22:14.270 --> 22:15.920
The Second Bureau is having a hard time now.

494
22:15.920 --> 22:18.360
Why did Long Yun, Chiang Kai-shek, and Xue Yue

495
22:18.360 --> 22:21.330
suddenly change the codebook for their communications?

496
22:21.330 --> 22:23.370
We're currently at a critical moment.

497
22:23.370 --> 22:25.730
Losing real-time knowledge of the enemy's movements

498
22:25.730 --> 22:27.930
will make it even more difficult for us.

499
22:31.840 --> 22:32.860
Take a break. I'll do it.

500
22:32.860 --> 22:35.190
It's fine. I'll just treat it as exercise.

501
22:36.290 --> 22:37.550
You're just stubborn.

502
22:39.160 --> 22:40.090
Go to sleep.

503
22:41.200 --> 22:42.430
Staying up is useless.

504
22:42.430 --> 22:44.510
Your eyes are as red as a rabbit's.

505
22:45.070 --> 22:46.670
If anyone should sleep, it's you.

506
22:46.670 --> 22:48.710
Your eyes are more bloodshot than anyone else's.

507
22:48.710 --> 22:50.620
If we can't cross the Jinsha River,

508
22:50.620 --> 22:52.420
none of us can sleep peacefully.

509
22:56.670 --> 22:57.600
Chen Changfeng.

510
22:57.610 --> 22:58.330
Here.

511
22:58.700 --> 22:59.510
Go to sleep.

512
23:01.400 --> 23:02.260
I'm not sleepy.

513
23:08.330 --> 23:09.130
We cracked it!

514
23:14.660 --> 23:15.180
Report.

515
23:15.350 --> 23:15.920
Leaders,

516
23:16.090 --> 23:18.150
we have cracked the enemy's new code.

517
23:18.200 --> 23:19.060
You cracked it?

518
23:26.770 --> 23:27.680
Great.

519
23:29.440 --> 23:31.770
We also found the reason why Long Yun changed the code.

520
23:31.770 --> 23:32.500
What happened?

521
23:32.500 --> 23:34.160
Please look at this telegram.

522
23:34.270 --> 23:36.050
This is from Long Yun to Chiang Kai-shek.

523
23:36.050 --> 23:37.170
He suggested to Chiang Kai-shek

524
23:37.170 --> 23:39.330
to compile and print more sets of codebooks

525
23:39.330 --> 23:41.190
and use a different one every day.

526
23:41.350 --> 23:42.190
If so,

527
23:42.440 --> 23:43.830
wouldn't it be even more difficult for us

528
23:43.830 --> 23:44.960
to crack the enemy's code?

529
23:44.960 --> 23:45.760
Don't worry.

530
23:46.160 --> 23:46.880
I think this is just

531
23:46.880 --> 23:48.540
Long Yun's wishful thinking.

532
23:48.930 --> 23:51.010
He now demands a new code every day.

533
23:51.200 --> 23:53.330
He can't even compile that many codes.

534
23:53.330 --> 23:54.850
Even if he could,

535
23:54.940 --> 23:56.780
with the KMT troops currently pursuing us

536
23:56.780 --> 23:58.090
having dozens of radio stations,

537
23:58.090 --> 24:01.210
he wouldn't even be able to deliver the codebooks in time.

538
24:01.210 --> 24:02.530
Please rest assured, Commander-in-Chief.

539
24:02.530 --> 24:04.390
The faster the enemy changes their cipher,

540
24:04.390 --> 24:06.520
the faster our Second Bureau decodes it.

541
24:06.520 --> 24:07.710
We firmly guarantee that the Military Commission

542
24:07.710 --> 24:08.940
will keep track of enemy movements in time.

543
24:08.940 --> 24:09.420
Good.

544
24:09.580 --> 24:11.420
With your words, I am relieved.

545
24:13.150 --> 24:14.150
Comrade Xisheng.

546
24:14.600 --> 24:16.040
With your Second Bureau here,

547
24:16.040 --> 24:18.380
it's like we're walking at night with a lantern,

548
24:18.380 --> 24:20.310
seeing everything crystal clear.

549
24:20.470 --> 24:21.640
In the past few months,

550
24:21.640 --> 24:23.610
we have always been able to shake off the pursuing enemy,

551
24:23.610 --> 24:25.810
thanks largely to the Second Bureau.

552
24:27.500 --> 24:28.080
Here.

553
24:30.430 --> 24:32.140
Actually, the role of our Second Bureau

554
24:32.140 --> 24:33.140
is not that great.

555
24:33.510 --> 24:35.000
In the 1st Counter-Encirclement Campaign,

556
24:35.000 --> 24:36.420
we didn't even have the Second Bureau.

557
24:36.420 --> 24:38.210
We only had half a radio station then.

558
24:38.210 --> 24:39.770
During the 2nd and 3rd Counter-Encirclement Campaigns,

559
24:39.770 --> 24:42.860
we could only judge through the radio

560
24:42.890 --> 24:45.750
the position of the enemy's Division-level units,

561
24:45.960 --> 24:48.080
and we couldn't completely decode the cipher.

562
24:48.080 --> 24:50.530
But our Red Army still won battles.

563
24:50.830 --> 24:52.590
During the 5th Counter-Encirclement Campaign,

564
24:52.590 --> 24:54.350
we had completely decoded

565
24:54.790 --> 24:56.000
the enemy's secret telegrams.

566
24:56.000 --> 24:58.460
But under the wrong command of Comrade Li De,

567
24:58.720 --> 25:00.780
didn't we still lose the Soviet area?

568
25:01.150 --> 25:02.910
It seems that the key to victory

569
25:03.030 --> 25:05.130
still relies on correct military command.

570
25:05.130 --> 25:06.130
Comrade Xisheng,

571
25:06.320 --> 25:08.320
don't just be modest at this time.

572
25:08.800 --> 25:10.200
You should brag a little.

573
25:10.890 --> 25:12.240
You can brag about this.

574
25:12.520 --> 25:14.450
The contribution of your Second Bureau is obvious to all,

575
25:14.450 --> 25:15.690
and this is the proof.

576
25:17.950 --> 25:19.410
As for the enemy's cipher,

577
25:19.430 --> 25:22.220
there are rules to follow when decoding it,

578
25:22.240 --> 25:23.570
so it's not that difficult.

579
25:23.570 --> 25:24.830
What's truly impressive

580
25:24.830 --> 25:25.790
is the "Hao Cipher" devised

581
25:25.790 --> 25:27.330
by Vice Chairman Zhou himself.

582
25:27.330 --> 25:28.810
From 1931 to now,

583
25:28.860 --> 25:30.410
it has never been decoded by the enemy.

584
25:30.410 --> 25:31.870
Enemy ciphers come and go,

585
25:32.070 --> 25:33.390
but the "Hao Cipher" stands firm.

586
25:33.390 --> 25:36.460
Enlai is truly a cipher warfare expert.

587
25:37.730 --> 25:38.920
I wouldn't dare say that.

588
25:38.920 --> 25:41.960
When the radio station in Hong Kong was destroyed by the enemy,

589
25:41.960 --> 25:42.960
without a cipher,

590
25:42.980 --> 25:44.430
we couldn't make any contact.

591
25:44.430 --> 25:45.840
I was forced to do it,

592
25:45.890 --> 25:47.330
and had no choice.

593
25:48.110 --> 25:51.240
Enlai's modesty is even more excessive than Xisheng's.

594
25:53.130 --> 25:54.200
Report!

595
25:56.710 --> 25:58.840
Report, a telegram from the 9th Corps.

596
26:07.160 --> 26:07.880
Good news.

597
26:07.940 --> 26:08.550
At dusk,

598
26:08.860 --> 26:11.080
the 9th Corps once again, without shedding blood,

599
26:11.080 --> 26:12.680
occupied Dongchuan County.

600
26:12.770 --> 26:14.000
They mobilized the masses overnight,

601
26:14.000 --> 26:16.300
and raised nearly 100,000 silver dollars,

602
26:16.300 --> 26:17.820
over 400 bolts of cloth,

603
26:18.270 --> 26:19.830
over 300 guns,

604
26:20.070 --> 26:21.700
and over 20,000 rounds of ammunition.

605
26:21.700 --> 26:23.490
From Xuanwei to Dongchuan,

606
26:23.870 --> 26:26.830
they expanded the Red Army by nearly 2,000 people.

607
26:28.270 --> 26:29.270
This Luo Binghui,

608
26:29.270 --> 26:31.130
a Corps Commander born as a slave,

609
26:31.340 --> 26:33.110
is like a fish in water when he returns to his hometown.

610
26:33.110 --> 26:34.440
He understands people's hearts and has appeal.

611
26:34.440 --> 26:35.880
He is our strategic light cavalry.

612
26:35.880 --> 26:37.920
Taking 2 cities without shedding blood,

613
26:37.920 --> 26:38.860
he not only pinned down the enemy

614
26:38.860 --> 26:40.160
but also expanded his own strength.

615
26:40.160 --> 26:40.890
Amazing.

616
26:40.990 --> 26:42.050
They also asked the Military Commission for instructions,

617
26:42.050 --> 26:43.850
planning to cross the river around the 4th

618
26:43.850 --> 26:47.370
in the Menggu area of Dongchuan.

619
26:47.920 --> 26:48.640
Look.

620
26:49.130 --> 26:51.200
They're crossing the river downstream,

621
26:51.200 --> 26:53.800
further confusing and pinning down the enemy.

622
26:54.160 --> 26:54.720
Now,

623
26:54.780 --> 26:56.890
our strategic space has been opened up.

624
26:56.890 --> 26:58.100
It all depends on whether

625
26:58.100 --> 27:00.430
Bocheng can find boats at Jiaoping Ferry.

626
27:01.310 --> 27:02.440
Jiaoping Ferry.

627
27:02.690 --> 27:03.620
Report!

628
27:08.030 --> 27:08.880
Leaders.

629
27:09.800 --> 27:11.800
Chief of Staff Bocheng sent a telegram.

630
27:11.800 --> 27:12.750
On their way,

631
27:13.090 --> 27:14.710
they captured a Yunnan Army soldier.

632
27:14.710 --> 27:16.230
They seized an order on him

633
27:16.130 --> 27:17.990
[Wang Zheng, Director of the Third Bureau of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission]

634
27:16.450 --> 27:18.440
about the Yunnan Army burning the ferry boats.

635
27:18.440 --> 27:21.370
The current situation at Jiaoping Ferry is unknown.

636
27:28.090 --> 27:29.020
Go back and rest.

637
27:29.180 --> 27:29.780
All right.

638
27:46.770 --> 27:47.600
Changfeng,

639
27:48.090 --> 27:48.810
go to sleep.

640
27:48.850 --> 27:50.970
Chairman, we still have to stand guard for you.

641
27:50.970 --> 27:51.870
Go to sleep!

642
27:53.040 --> 27:55.100
Dying of exhaustion is not glorious!

643
27:57.670 --> 27:59.150
[Chen Changfeng, Mao Zedong's Guard]

644
27:58.740 --> 27:59.430
Yes, sir.

645
29:00.480 --> 29:05.060
[Jiaoping Ferry, Jinsha, Yunnan]

646
29:21.130 --> 29:21.860
Minister Li.

647
29:22.160 --> 29:23.620
There's a boat over there.

648
29:24.090 --> 29:25.890
I'll take some men over to check the situation first.

649
29:25.890 --> 29:26.530
Wait.

650
29:26.980 --> 29:28.510
The boatmen are civilians.

651
29:28.720 --> 29:29.720
I'd better go.

652
29:30.200 --> 29:31.600
Send a squad to keep watch

653
29:31.830 --> 29:32.950
in case anyone returns.

654
29:32.950 --> 29:33.530
Yes, sir.

655
29:34.240 --> 29:36.170
Squad One, go over and stand guard.

656
29:48.790 --> 29:50.320
I've made up my mind, Uncle.

657
29:50.460 --> 29:53.060
When I go back, I'll quit my job with Master Lin.

658
29:53.680 --> 29:56.330
Chaoshou, you have to think it through.

659
29:57.250 --> 29:59.010
It's chaotic out there.

660
29:59.180 --> 30:00.710
It's hard enough just to stay alive.

661
30:00.710 --> 30:01.860
Besides,

662
30:02.580 --> 30:05.300
the river defense brigades are all burning boats now.

663
30:05.300 --> 30:06.970
If you quit,

664
30:07.260 --> 30:09.520
we won't be able to keep this boat either.

665
30:09.560 --> 30:11.230
If we can't keep it, let them burn it.

666
30:11.230 --> 30:12.760
We brave the wind and waves.

667
30:12.870 --> 30:13.740
All year round,

668
30:14.100 --> 30:14.680
the tax bureau

669
30:14.680 --> 30:16.080
only gives us a few bucks.

670
30:16.140 --> 30:18.450
They either delay payment or find ways to deduct it.

671
30:18.450 --> 30:20.980
Meanwhile, they eat and drink well every day.

672
30:21.220 --> 30:22.820
My mom got sick in the spring.

673
30:22.940 --> 30:24.650
We had no money and couldn't afford treatment.

674
30:24.650 --> 30:26.050
That bastard Master Lin.

675
30:26.120 --> 30:27.650
I knelt down and begged him,

676
30:27.690 --> 30:29.710
but he wouldn't even give me one dollar.

677
30:29.710 --> 30:33.040
My mom died because her treatment was delayed.

678
30:35.170 --> 30:36.090
What a world.

679
30:36.400 --> 30:37.460
Fellow villagers.

680
30:37.950 --> 30:39.010
Fellow villagers.

681
30:41.640 --> 30:42.470
Excuse me.

682
30:43.210 --> 30:45.270
Please help us cross the river today.

683
30:45.560 --> 30:46.570
I'll pay in cash.

684
30:52.510 --> 30:53.270
Officer,

685
30:53.720 --> 30:56.050
our boat was chartered by other officers.

686
30:56.430 --> 30:58.100
When those two officers come back later,

687
30:58.100 --> 30:58.970
they still need to take the boat.

688
30:58.970 --> 30:59.580
I'm afraid

689
31:00.400 --> 31:02.130
they won't be able to come back.

690
31:04.110 --> 31:06.150
Who... who are you?

691
31:06.310 --> 31:07.440
I am from the Red Army.

692
31:07.440 --> 31:08.160
The Red Army?

693
31:08.160 --> 31:08.780
Yes.

694
31:09.640 --> 31:11.320
What, haven't you heard of us?

695
31:12.290 --> 31:14.280
I've heard of you. I know.

696
31:15.140 --> 31:15.680
But...

697
31:15.710 --> 31:18.270
But they all say we are monsters.

698
31:18.290 --> 31:18.940
Right?

699
31:23.570 --> 31:24.320
It's okay.

700
31:24.510 --> 31:26.440
Come, fellow villagers. Sit down.

701
31:26.570 --> 31:27.080
Sit.

702
31:29.940 --> 31:32.070
We Red Army soldiers are just like you.

703
31:32.510 --> 31:34.270
We all come from poor backgrounds.

704
31:34.270 --> 31:36.590
We are an army fighting for the poor.

705
31:36.870 --> 31:38.740
We are here to strike

706
31:38.910 --> 31:41.190
the Kuomintang reactionaries across the river,

707
31:41.190 --> 31:42.590
and stand up for the poor.

708
31:46.750 --> 31:47.380
Is it true?

709
31:47.830 --> 31:48.960
Of course it's true.

710
31:52.150 --> 31:54.070
I heard you chatting just now.

711
31:54.750 --> 31:57.280
There's a tax bureau across the river, right?

712
31:58.000 --> 31:59.460
How many people are there?

713
31:59.680 --> 32:01.610
They have 5 or 6 people,

714
32:01.990 --> 32:03.880
and a security team of over 30.

715
32:04.290 --> 32:05.350
They all have guns.

716
32:05.400 --> 32:07.660
Are there any other troops besides them?

717
32:08.070 --> 32:10.850
A Company of the Sichuan Army arrived early this morning.

718
32:10.850 --> 32:12.770
They are stationed behind the town,

719
32:12.770 --> 32:14.570
a few kilometers from the ferry.

720
32:16.580 --> 32:19.070
How many men are in your Red Army?

721
32:22.570 --> 32:23.970
Company Commander Xiao!

722
32:24.290 --> 32:24.920
Here!

723
32:26.390 --> 32:27.110
Follow me!

724
32:47.160 --> 32:47.920
Listen up!

725
32:48.110 --> 32:49.390
Halt!

726
32:50.430 --> 32:52.280
Left face!

727
32:55.260 --> 32:56.320
Fellow villagers.

728
32:56.720 --> 32:58.440
We need you to ferry us across the river

729
32:58.440 --> 33:00.570
so we can attack the tax bureau,

730
33:01.200 --> 33:03.120
the security team, and the Sichuan Army,

731
33:03.120 --> 33:04.560
and stand up for the poor

732
33:04.860 --> 33:06.300
and your mother.

733
33:07.850 --> 33:08.480
Uncle.

734
33:11.320 --> 33:13.070
We'll take this job.

735
33:13.750 --> 33:14.440
Great.

736
33:18.020 --> 33:19.510
This is the advance payment for the boat.

737
33:19.510 --> 33:21.710
I'll make up the rest if it's not enough.

738
33:24.530 --> 33:25.850
You really pay in cash?

739
33:25.960 --> 33:28.360
Of course. The Red Army keeps its word.

740
33:32.990 --> 33:35.280
You have so many people. One boat would take too long.

741
33:35.280 --> 33:37.600
What? You have another boat?

742
33:38.170 --> 33:39.900
I hid a broken boat over there.

743
33:40.170 --> 33:41.960
It can be used with a little repair.

744
33:41.960 --> 33:43.560
It's even bigger than this one.

745
33:43.560 --> 33:44.400
That's great.

746
33:44.720 --> 33:46.830
I'll send someone to help you push the boat.

747
33:46.830 --> 33:47.350
Okay.

748
33:47.440 --> 33:48.000
Good.

749
33:50.720 --> 33:52.360
Fellow villagers, this is really great.

750
33:52.360 --> 33:53.760
You've been a great help to us.

751
33:53.760 --> 33:54.990
You're welcome.

752
33:56.680 --> 33:57.340
Be careful.

753
33:57.360 --> 33:57.960
First Squad.

754
33:57.960 --> 33:58.610
Here!

755
33:59.110 --> 34:00.440
Help the fellow villagers tow the boat!

756
34:00.440 --> 34:01.160
Yes, sir!

757
34:01.550 --> 34:02.280
Company Commander Xiao.

758
34:02.280 --> 34:02.680
Here!

759
34:02.860 --> 34:04.660
Take 2 platoons and cross the river first.

760
34:04.660 --> 34:06.710
You must first control the ferry on the other side.

761
34:06.710 --> 34:09.060
Once successful, light a bonfire as a signal.

762
34:09.060 --> 34:11.850
Then advance in depth to wipe out that Sichuan Army Company.

763
34:11.850 --> 34:13.770
Light another bonfire after you succeed.

764
34:13.770 --> 34:15.340
I'll wait here until the main force arrives,

765
34:15.340 --> 34:17.150
and we will immediately cross the river to support you.

766
34:17.150 --> 34:17.960
Yes, sir!

767
34:18.239 --> 34:20.360
Attention all! Right face!

768
34:20.710 --> 34:21.929
Fellow villager, have a seat.

769
34:21.929 --> 34:23.409
Okay, okay.

770
34:35.270 --> 34:36.020
Be careful.

771
34:42.179 --> 34:43.889
Chief of Staff. There's a block here.

772
34:43.889 --> 34:44.449
Okay.

773
34:46.260 --> 34:46.739
Come.

774
34:48.320 --> 34:48.980
Be careful.

775
34:49.139 --> 34:50.159
There's a hole here.

776
34:50.159 --> 34:51.000
Watch your step back there.

777
34:51.000 --> 34:52.560
-Watch your step. -Let's go.

778
34:52.560 --> 34:54.420
Your eyesight is bad. Be careful.

779
34:54.719 --> 34:55.630
Don't worry.

780
34:56.050 --> 34:57.760
If you, Chen the cripple, can walk,

781
34:57.760 --> 35:00.020
I, Liu the blind, can naturally walk too.

782
35:01.170 --> 35:03.760
You might as well say my eyes work and your legs do,

783
35:03.760 --> 35:05.690
so together we'd get there faster.

784
35:05.770 --> 35:06.520
Right.

785
35:11.570 --> 35:12.220
Who is it?

786
35:12.290 --> 35:13.020
The river...

787
35:13.710 --> 35:14.510
is turbulent.

788
35:20.050 --> 35:20.580
Leaders.

789
35:20.600 --> 35:21.740
Regiment Commander, Political Commissar.

790
35:21.740 --> 35:23.130
Our company found 2 boats.

791
35:23.130 --> 35:24.930
We are crossing the river to control the ferry on the other side.

792
35:24.930 --> 35:26.480
Minister Li asked me to welcome you.

793
35:26.480 --> 35:27.810
Li is anxious.

794
35:27.910 --> 35:28.710
Great.

795
35:29.120 --> 35:30.450
It's good to have boats.

796
35:30.510 --> 35:31.710
Chen Geng, Renqiong,

797
35:31.960 --> 35:33.020
let's walk faster.

798
35:33.030 --> 35:33.480
Okay.

799
35:34.000 --> 35:35.480
Comrades, try harder.

800
35:35.590 --> 35:36.480
Move faster!

801
35:36.510 --> 35:37.280
Let's go.

802
36:06.190 --> 36:09.750
[Tax Bureau]

803
36:19.730 --> 36:20.770
Master Lin.

804
36:22.550 --> 36:23.630
Master Lin.

805
36:24.780 --> 36:26.220
Master Lin, open the door.

806
36:26.220 --> 36:27.230
Which bastard

807
36:27.250 --> 36:28.840
is yelling in the middle of the night?

808
36:28.840 --> 36:29.920
Master Lin, it's me.

809
36:29.920 --> 36:30.920
I'm Chaoshou.

810
36:31.170 --> 36:32.230
It's you, bastard.

811
36:32.460 --> 36:33.520
What's the matter?

812
36:33.700 --> 36:36.100
A group of merchants from Yunnan just crossed the river.

813
36:36.100 --> 36:37.310
They want to pay taxes.

814
36:37.310 --> 36:38.500
What taxes are they paying?

815
36:38.500 --> 36:40.380
Look what time it is.

816
36:41.740 --> 36:43.070
Tell him there are pigs.

817
36:44.570 --> 36:45.650
If it's too late for you,

818
36:45.650 --> 36:47.040
I'll tell them to leave.

819
36:47.360 --> 36:49.950
What a pity, more than a dozen big fat pigs.

820
36:50.840 --> 36:51.720
Wait a minute.

821
37:00.340 --> 37:01.740
Who wants to pay taxes?

822
37:03.280 --> 37:03.880
Me.

823
37:04.460 --> 37:05.340
Red Army.

824
37:09.460 --> 37:10.370
Be careful.

825
37:10.680 --> 37:11.870
Renqiong. Help him.

826
37:12.720 --> 37:13.640
Be careful.

827
37:13.660 --> 37:14.190
Let's go.

828
37:15.340 --> 37:16.540
You're finally here.

829
37:17.220 --> 37:18.150
Comrade Kenong.

830
37:20.360 --> 37:21.240
How is it?

831
37:22.070 --> 37:23.400
The 5th Company has controlled the ferry.

832
37:23.400 --> 37:25.040
Jiaoping Ferry is now in our hands.

833
37:25.040 --> 37:26.410
Great.

834
37:27.440 --> 37:28.280
Comrades.

835
37:28.750 --> 37:32.390
The main force of the Military Commission will cross the river from here.

836
37:32.390 --> 37:34.960
It's not enough for us to just control the ferry.

837
37:34.960 --> 37:36.320
Twenty kilometers north of the opposite bank,

838
37:36.320 --> 37:38.510
there is a market town called Tong'an Prefecture.

839
37:38.510 --> 37:39.660
The terrain there is dangerous,

840
37:39.660 --> 37:42.060
controlling the road to Huili County.

841
37:43.000 --> 37:43.880
My idea is that

842
37:44.270 --> 37:46.040
the main force of the Cadre Regiment crosses the river overnight

843
37:46.040 --> 37:47.590
to seize Tong'an Prefecture,

844
37:47.590 --> 37:48.750
ensuring the safety of the Military Commission Column

845
37:48.750 --> 37:50.210
after crossing the river.

846
37:50.690 --> 37:51.890
But this way,

847
37:52.690 --> 37:53.870
comrades won't get any rest.

848
37:53.870 --> 37:55.000
It will be very hard.

849
37:55.280 --> 37:56.590
Don't worry, Chief of Staff.

850
37:56.590 --> 37:57.480
The Cadre Regiment has long been ready

851
37:57.480 --> 37:58.940
for continuous fighting.

852
37:59.880 --> 38:01.510
Just give the order.

853
38:02.320 --> 38:03.400
We will resolutely execute it.

854
38:03.400 --> 38:03.840
Right.

855
38:04.460 --> 38:05.180
Okay.

856
38:07.400 --> 38:08.400
The boat is back.

857
38:09.150 --> 38:09.680
Let's go.

858
38:10.000 --> 38:10.710
Let's go.

859
38:11.110 --> 38:11.760
Let's go.

860
38:12.440 --> 38:13.440
Fellow villager.

861
38:14.000 --> 38:14.670
Chaoshou.

862
38:15.190 --> 38:16.590
Thank you for your hard work.

863
38:16.590 --> 38:17.760
Not at all.

864
38:18.440 --> 38:20.150
You all need to cross the river?

865
38:20.150 --> 38:20.710
Yes.

866
38:20.880 --> 38:22.540
Let's settle the bill in cash.

867
38:22.760 --> 38:23.920
Is that okay with you?

868
38:23.920 --> 38:25.820
You've already given me 5 silver dollars.

869
38:25.820 --> 38:27.780
This time, I can do it for free.

870
38:28.320 --> 38:29.400
We can go now.

871
38:29.670 --> 38:30.580
That boat is small.

872
38:30.580 --> 38:31.980
Everyone, get on my boat.

873
38:32.110 --> 38:33.860
Thank you for your trouble, fellow villager.

874
38:33.860 --> 38:35.990
It's no trouble. Get on board quickly.

875
38:36.410 --> 38:37.960
Comrades, get on board.

876
38:39.560 --> 38:41.040
Let's go.

877
38:41.270 --> 38:42.750
This way, this way.

878
38:44.590 --> 38:45.470
Be careful.

879
38:47.150 --> 38:47.810
Be careful.

880
38:48.150 --> 38:49.150
Go this way. Good.

881
38:49.400 --> 38:50.030
Good.

882
38:50.760 --> 38:51.550
Come, sit.

883
38:59.380 --> 39:00.220
Comrades.

884
39:01.030 --> 39:02.260
We have a heavy task ahead.

885
39:02.260 --> 39:04.300
Let's hurry up and eat something

886
39:05.350 --> 39:06.750
to replenish our energy.

887
39:07.670 --> 39:08.320
Come on.

888
39:08.360 --> 39:08.840
Come on.

889
39:08.920 --> 39:10.450
Hurry up and eat something.

890
39:12.150 --> 39:12.920
Here.

891
39:13.820 --> 39:14.260
Okay.

892
39:21.560 --> 39:23.240
Here, young fellow villager, have a potato.

893
39:23.240 --> 39:24.100
I don't want it.

894
39:24.260 --> 39:24.610
Here.

895
39:25.100 --> 39:25.480
Here.

896
39:25.500 --> 39:26.500
Thank you.

897
39:38.990 --> 39:39.550
Sir.

898
39:40.710 --> 39:42.000
You're also from Sichuan?

899
39:42.000 --> 39:42.800
That's right.

900
39:43.150 --> 39:44.630
I'm from Kai County, Sichuan.

901
39:44.630 --> 39:46.540
Although my hometown is a bit far from yours,

902
39:46.540 --> 39:49.020
we Sichuan people are all one family.

903
39:49.550 --> 39:52.350
People from Sichuan and Chongqing are one family.

904
39:52.670 --> 39:53.920
You're such a high-ranking official,

905
39:53.920 --> 39:55.230
but you don't put on airs at all.

906
39:55.230 --> 39:56.880
We all come from poor backgrounds.

907
39:56.880 --> 39:58.320
Officers and soldiers are equal.

908
39:58.320 --> 39:59.580
We eat from the same pot

909
39:59.590 --> 40:01.000
and sleep on the same bedboards.

910
40:01.000 --> 40:02.530
Who would we put on airs for?

911
40:02.930 --> 40:05.260
You Red Army soldiers are really amazing.

912
40:05.760 --> 40:07.270
That Master Lin from the tax bureau

913
40:07.270 --> 40:08.510
is just a petty official,

914
40:08.510 --> 40:09.800
but he's so arrogant.

915
40:10.320 --> 40:11.450
When it comes to us poor folks,

916
40:11.450 --> 40:13.530
he curses us at the drop of a hat and hits us whenever he pleases.

917
40:13.530 --> 40:15.230
That's why we need to teach him a lesson,

918
40:15.230 --> 40:16.000
so that he won't

919
40:16.000 --> 40:17.470
dare to bully the poor anymore.

920
40:17.470 --> 40:18.240
And also,

921
40:18.670 --> 40:21.020
we won't just deal with this one Master Lin.

922
40:21.020 --> 40:22.810
We'll deal with all those who oppress the common people,

923
40:22.810 --> 40:25.010
including local tyrants, evil gentry,

924
40:25.070 --> 40:26.280
and wicked landlords.

925
40:26.280 --> 40:27.760
Good, good.

926
40:29.190 --> 40:30.520
Young fellow villager.

927
40:31.150 --> 40:34.360
How many people can this boat hold when fully loaded?

928
40:34.510 --> 40:35.480
My boat is big.

929
40:35.760 --> 40:37.710
It can hold 30 people when full.

930
40:37.940 --> 40:39.340
My uncle's boat is small.

931
40:39.670 --> 40:41.650
It can hold 11 or 12 people without a problem.

932
40:41.650 --> 40:43.120
Can your bodies handle

933
40:43.600 --> 40:44.890
ferrying all of us across?

934
40:44.890 --> 40:47.510
We've been navigating the Jinsha River since we were kids.

935
40:47.510 --> 40:48.840
We're used to it.

936
40:49.400 --> 40:50.330
Skilled boatmen

937
40:50.590 --> 40:53.120
don't use brute force, but borrow the water's momentum.

938
40:53.120 --> 40:55.080
They know how to use skill.

939
40:56.790 --> 40:57.850
Kenong, Chen Geng.

940
40:59.110 --> 41:00.450
We still have too few boats.

941
41:00.450 --> 41:01.600
When we get to the opposite bank,

942
41:01.600 --> 41:03.600
we need to find a way to get more boats

943
41:04.010 --> 41:06.010
and find some more skilled boatmen.

944
41:06.490 --> 41:08.370
We need to ensure the main force can cross the river as soon as possible.

945
41:08.370 --> 41:08.850
Okay.

946
41:09.610 --> 41:10.480
Sir.

947
41:11.000 --> 41:13.440
Are there more troops behind you waiting to cross the river?

948
41:13.440 --> 41:14.030
Yes.

949
41:14.410 --> 41:15.940
We have thousands of troops

950
41:16.020 --> 41:17.950
waiting to cross the Jinsha River.

951
41:18.070 --> 41:19.800
Then I'll go find boats for you.

952
41:19.880 --> 41:20.340
Really?

953
41:20.360 --> 41:21.050
No problem.

954
41:21.920 --> 41:22.580
Be careful.

955
41:22.750 --> 41:23.670
Chaoshou,

956
41:24.140 --> 41:25.590
can you really find more boats?

957
41:25.590 --> 41:26.280
Yes.

958
41:26.440 --> 41:29.500
A while ago, Liu Yuantang sent troops to burn the boats.

959
41:29.520 --> 41:31.960
Our village and nearby villages hid a few.

960
41:32.470 --> 41:33.870
The boatmen are poor folks like me.

961
41:33.870 --> 41:34.690
I know them all.

962
41:34.690 --> 41:36.020
After I take you across,

963
41:36.090 --> 41:38.220
I'll rush over overnight to find them.

964
41:38.270 --> 41:38.940
I guarantee

965
41:39.450 --> 41:42.050
I'll bring both the people and the boats to you.

966
41:42.160 --> 41:42.670
That's great.

967
41:42.670 --> 41:43.370
If you do this,

968
41:43.370 --> 41:45.100
you'll be doing us a huge favor.

969
41:46.510 --> 41:48.360
We are family, right?

970
41:48.510 --> 41:51.710
Right. People from Sichuan and Chongqing are one family.

971
42:27.390 --> 42:28.390
Just now,

972
42:28.880 --> 42:31.410
I seemed to hear someone shouting in my dream,

973
42:31.730 --> 42:32.890
"There're boats!"

974
42:33.960 --> 42:35.080
In my dream,

975
42:35.900 --> 42:37.900
I also heard someone shouting that.

976
42:39.550 --> 42:42.900
I seemed to hear it in my dream too.

977
42:42.920 --> 42:44.850
Four people having the same dream.

978
42:47.320 --> 42:48.510
Is that possible?

979
42:57.070 --> 42:58.400
There're boats!

980
42:59.870 --> 43:01.190
There're boats!

981
43:02.800 --> 43:04.240
Am I still dreaming now?
